  "body": "Split out of #2389 (P1). The generation side of #2389 is fixed on `issue/2389-tilt-heights-axis`: a tilted operation's reference heights (Top/Bottom of stock, Top/Bottom of model, Work offset) are now read along the turned tool axis (`camcraft_app::operation::fold_height`). The display was not changed there.\n\nWhat still happens (from #2389's investigation):\n- `crates/ui/src/interact.rs` `height_planes` / `height_plane_lines` draw the Clearance/Retract/Top/Bottom planes as horizontal rectangles at the setup Z, across the stock's XY box. They do not read the tilt.\n- `crates/ui/src/operations.rs` `height_echo` prints \"(= Z ...)\" from `resolve_height`, the setup-Z resolve. For a tilted op on an asymmetric stock this number is not the value generation uses.\n- `operation::region_z` (used by `interact.rs`, `boundary_viz.rs`, `boundary_draft.rs`) also reads the setup Z for a tilted op.\n\nExpected: for a tilted op, each plane stands at right angles to the tool axis, at the distance `fold_height(...) - origin.z` along it from the plane origin, over the stock's extent in the plane's local XY (`TiltedFrame::to_world`). The echo states the value along the tool axis (e.g. \"(= 5.000 along tool axis)\") from the same `fold_height` call generation makes.\n\nRepro: `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj`, \"Flat A90\" > Heights tab (the planes lie flat above the bar). On that symmetric bar the numbers agree; on an asymmetric stock (#2390) they do not.\n\nDone means: the viewport planes and the \"(= ...)\" text of a tilted op use the op's frame and `fold_height`; a ui law test pins a tilted plane's corners and the echo value on an asymmetric stock; untilted planes and text unchanged.\n",
